@Vitalita.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5240

### OpenAPI document (Spanish)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: es

### Unknown route: 404 ProblemDetails with "message", localized in Spanish
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: es
Origin: http://localhost:5173

### Same request in English (default culture)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json

### CORS preflight from the Vite dev server
OPTIONS {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

### IAM: sign up (Caregiver by default). 201 + Location; 409 if the email exists; 400 if role=Admin
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: es

{
  "email": "andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123",
  "role": "Caregiver"
}

### IAM: sign up as Admin is rejected with 400
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not.an.admin@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### IAM: sign in. 200 with id, email, role, status and token; 401 for wrong credentials or inactive account
# @name signIn
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123"
}

### IAM: public email lookup. Array with zero or one {id, email}
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users?email=andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe
Accept: application/json

### IAM: get a user by id (Bearer token; own user or Admin)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users/{{signIn.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### IAM: sign in as the administrator seeded from Authentication:Admin (user-secrets)
# @name adminSignIn
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "<Authentication:Admin:Email>",
  "password": "<Authentication:Admin:Password>"
}

### IAM: list every user (Admin only; 401 without token, 403 for other roles)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminSignIn.response.body.token}}

### IAM: create a user with any role (Admin only). 201 + Location
# @name createdUser
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminSignIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "email": "renzo.rodriguez@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123",
  "role": "FamilyMember"
}

### IAM: replace a user (Admin, or the user themselves without changing role/status). password is optional
PUT {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users/{{createdUser.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminSignIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "email": "renzo.rodriguez@vitalita.pe",
  "role": "FamilyMember",
  "status": "Active",
  "password": null
}

### IAM: deactivate a user (logical delete, Admin only). 204; afterwards its sign-in returns 401
DELETE {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users/{{createdUser.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminSignIn.response.body.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Profiles. Full flow in one command: ./scripts/profiles-flow.sh
### The requests below use the caregiver signed in with "signIn" (andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe, role Caregiver).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Profiles: create the caregiver profile (own userId, role Caregiver). 201 + Location; 409 if it exists
# @name caregiverProfile
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/caregiver-profiles
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: es
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "userId": {{signIn.response.body.id}},
  "firstName": "Andrea",
  "lastName": "Mendoza",
  "phoneNumber": "987654321",
  "professionalTitle": "Licenciada en Enfermería",
  "bio": "Enfermera con 12 años de experiencia en cuidado geriátrico domiciliario.",
  "photoUrl": "",
  "certifications": ["Cuidado geriátrico", "Primeros auxilios"]
}

### Profiles: caregiver profile of a user (array with zero or one element; own user or Admin)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/caregiver-profiles?userId={{signIn.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### Profiles: replace the caregiver profile (owner only; userId cannot change)
PUT {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/caregiver-profiles/{{caregiverProfile.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "userId": {{signIn.response.body.id}},
  "firstName": "Andrea",
  "lastName": "Mendoza Ríos",
  "phoneNumber": "987654321",
  "professionalTitle": "Licenciada en Enfermería",
  "bio": "",
  "photoUrl": "",
  "certifications": ["Cuidado geriátrico"]
}

### Profiles: register an older adult (caregiverId = own caregiver profile). birthDate is yyyy-MM-dd
# @name olderAdult
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/older-adults
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: es
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "caregiverId": {{caregiverProfile.response.body.id}},
  "firstName": "María",
  "lastName": "Rodríguez",
  "birthDate": "1948-03-12",
  "documentNumber": "40218463",
  "bloodType": "O+",
  "allergies": ["Penicilina"],
  "chronicConditions": ["Hipertensión arterial", "Diabetes tipo 2"],
  "emergencyContact": { "name": "Renzo Rodríguez", "phoneNumber": "987111222", "relationship": "Son" },
  "observations": "Requiere asistencia para caminar distancias largas.",
  "status": "Active"
}

### Profiles: invalid older adult. 400 with localized errors per field
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/older-adults
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: es
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "caregiverId": {{caregiverProfile.response.body.id}},
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Rodríguez",
  "birthDate": "2099-01-01",
  "documentNumber": "123",
  "bloodType": "Z+"
}

### Profiles: older adults of the caregiver (403 for another caregiver profile)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/older-adults?caregiverId={{caregiverProfile.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### Profiles: older adults by ids (the ones the requester cannot read are left out)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/older-adults?id={{olderAdult.response.body.id}}&id=999
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### Profiles: archive the older adult (PUT with the whole resource; status is required)
PUT {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/older-adults/{{olderAdult.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "caregiverId": {{caregiverProfile.response.body.id}},
  "firstName": "María",
  "lastName": "Rodríguez",
  "birthDate": "1948-03-12",
  "documentNumber": "40218463",
  "bloodType": "O+",
  "allergies": ["Penicilina"],
  "chronicConditions": ["Hipertensión arterial"],
  "emergencyContact": { "name": "Renzo Rodríguez", "phoneNumber": "987111222", "relationship": "Son" },
  "observations": "",
  "status": "Active"
}

### Profiles: invite a family member. The server generates the code (VITA- + 8) and the dates; 409 if already invited
# @name invitation
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/family-access
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "olderAdultId": {{olderAdult.response.body.id}},
  "invitedEmail": "carla.rodriguez@correo.pe",
  "relationship": "Daughter"
}

### Profiles: public invitation lookup (no token). [invitation] when pending and not expired; [] otherwise
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/family-access?invitationCode={{invitation.response.body.invitationCode}}
Accept: application/json

### Profiles: accesses of an older adult (caregiver in charge)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/family-access?olderAdultId={{olderAdult.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### Profiles: revoke the invitation (caregiver in charge). Revoked is final: changing it again returns 409
PUT {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/family-access/{{invitation.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

{
  "status": "Revoked",
  "familyMemberId": null,
  "relationship": "Daughter"
}

### Profiles: family member steps (sign up with the invited email, sign in, POST /family-member-profiles and
### PUT /family-access/{id} with status Active and the own familyMemberId) are in ./scripts/profiles-flow.sh.
